            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_012.html",
            "paragraph": 1,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 5 Thursday, December 26",
            "page": "11",
            "text": "CHAPTER 5 Thursday, December 26\nFor the first time since he began his monologue, the old man had managed to take Blomkvist by surprise. He had to ask him to repeat it to be sure he had heard correctly. Nothing in the cuttings had hinted at a murder.\n“It was September 24, 1966. Harriet was sixteen and had just begun her second year at prep school. It was a Saturday, and it turned into the worst day of my life. I’ve gone over the events so many times that I think I can account for what happened in every minute of that day—except the most important thing.”",
            "paragraph_end": 3,
            "part_end": 1,
            "embedding_model": "sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1",
            "source_id": "555dc56c42176fe8382deca228ac6f72f60bd96e8f96846f0cc94dfc0f6b8284",
            "id": "555dc56c-4217-6fe8-382d-eca228ac6f72",
